# Emergent society
#
# Nothing below tells anybody what to do.  There is no schedule, no policy, no
# social algorithm: only four people, what they have, what they need, and how
# they start out feeling about each other.
#
# Every tick each agent scores every action it could take against the charge on
# the relevant edge of the field and takes the strongest one.  Rivalries,
# alliances, isolation and reconciliation are all downstream of that scoring --
# see `catharsis/actions.py` for the whole repertoire, which is a table, not a
# decision tree.
#
# Run it with --trace to watch the society happen:
#
#     catharsis run examples/society.catharsis --trace

agent alice bob charlie diana

# Scarcity. Charlie and Diana are short of what Alice and Bob are sitting on,
# which is enough to produce envy without anybody being told to be envious.
have alice bread 4
have bob bread 3
have charlie bread 0
have diana bread 1

need alice bread 1
need bob bread 1
need charlie bread 2
need diana bread 2

# Temperament: a baseline the self-loop is pulled back toward, forever.
trait alice pride 0.55
trait bob trust 0.45
trait charlie loneliness 0.60
trait diana curiosity 0.65

# The starting configuration. One couple, one outsider, one observer.
love alice bob 0.7
love bob alice 0.6
trust bob alice 0.7
jealousy charlie bob 0.6
lonely charlie 0.7
curious diana
fear diana charlie 0.4

tick 30

observe
